From: Local Patch <local@patch>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: sun8i: r40: bananapi-m2-ultra: Limit eMMC to 25MHz for stability

Limit the eMMC (mmc2) clock speed to 25MHz to ensure stable operation
in Legacy Mode. Although throughput is lower (~20MB/s), this guarantees
stability. Also explicitly declare 1.8V is not supported as a safety
precaution.

Signed-off-by: Local Patch <local@patch>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-r40-bananapi-m2-ultra.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-r40-bananapi-m2-ultra.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-r40-bananapi-m2-ultra.dts
@@ -211,6 +211,14 @@
 	bus-width = <8>;
 	non-removable;
 	status = "okay";
+
+	/* 1. Core solution: Limit physical clock speed. */
+	/* Cap the max frequency at 25MHz to ensure stable operation in Legacy Mode. */
+	/* Although throughput is lower (~20MB/s), this guarantees stability. */
+	max-frequency = <25000000>;
+
+	/* 2. Safety precaution: Explicitly declare 1.8V is not supported. */
+	no-1-8-v;
 };
 
 &ohci1 {
